 would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 39.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 18.8 to 95.2. December accounts for 0% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 8. Contract [1], for 39,247.39 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not prove that any of them were improperly awarded. It could be due to market pricing, budget constraints, or the need for multiple smaller contracts to meet specific requirements.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the reason for the amount. Also, review the contracts of awardee A to see if they are consistently awarded for similar needs or if there is a pattern in the types of work contracted. Look at the distribution of contracts across different months to see if there is a seasonal trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["Vt99t2c2%2BNp4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D","ERmEp3%2BnzbN4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D","s8I37Po7cd2opEMYCmrbmw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}